    "basis": "A run is a top-level session (subagents and sessions that rolled over are counted separately). Outcome follows Hermes: a run failed when it ended on a provider or agent error, and was cut off when it ended waiting on a tool or a reply. A scheduled run also failed when every tool call in it failed, even if Hermes booked it complete. Run time is start to end; Hermes records no per-call latency. Tool failures use the rule Hermes uses to mark failed tool calls. The trend compares these 30 days with the 30 days before them."
